{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Gather yourselves and I will tell you.</b> And it is written ״הקבצו ושמעו״ — here is a hint to them that they will go into exile twice and be gathered in both of them." "<b>That which will befall you.</b> This means at the end of four hundred and thirty years of the Egyptian exile, for the verses compel us to interpret thus — for if not, it should have written ״באחרית ימים״, at the end of the days of the world. And I have heard: באחרית הימים — of the Holy One, blessed be He, which is at the end of five thousand. Jacob sought to reveal the End, and the Shekhinah withdrew from him. He was astonished and said: Why — if these are not worthy to have the End revealed to them, is there no sin in them? That is, there is in all the names of the tribes neither chet nor tet. The Holy Spirit answered him: Also in all the letters of the names of the tribes there is neither qof nor tsadi — if so, they are not worthy to have the End revealed. ״ועל אשר קראת לבניך להם אתה קורא לי״ — you do not call. As it is said: ״ולא אותי קראת יעקב כי יגעת בי ישראל״ — this measure is not yours; ״הולך רכיל מגלה סוד״ etc. When Jacob saw this, he launched into words and said: ״ראובן בכורי אתה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:24.567284431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}